# v3.7 (review v11 N9) widened the closed binary set from {"git"} to {"git","env","sh","python3.12"} because the narrow set
# was a measured FALSE RED. v3.8 (review v12 B2) keeps the width but not the hole: the widening put three INTERPRETERS into
# the ordinary-tool set while provider recognition still compared EXACT argv ELEMENTS — and an interpreter's payload is a
# single element, so `/bin/sh -c '<runtime-assembled codex line>' … <neutral prompt>` was green. The set is therefore split.
# TOOLS carry free argv and are recognised by exact elements (a substring test would flag the ordinary
# `git show …:docs/loop/codex-evidence-contract.md`). WRAPPERS are interpreters: their whole argv is tested for provider
# markers as a SUBSTRING, and any argv element longer than WRAPPER_ARGV_MAX that is not one of the captured prompts is
# treated as a payload. Measured: the reference starts only `git`, and review v11's two false-red probes
# (`/usr/bin/env true`, `python3.12 -c 'print(1)'`) carry no marker and no long element — both stay green.
# v3.9 (review v13 B2): a basename is not an identity and an argv is not a payload. Six measured mutants were green
# under v3.8: `sh` with the script on STDIN (argv=['/bin/sh']), `sh -c 'exec "$0" "$@"'` with short elements, `env` with
# a short argv, `python3.12 -c` with a short one-liner, and — the worst — a shell script whose BASENAME is `git`, which
# the evidence file reported as `live_start_binaries=['git']`. One of them put
# `PROVIDER=codex PROMPT=read docs/loop/autonomous-loop-plan-v1.md` on a child's stdin while the gate was green.
# v3.9 therefore binds three things instead of the basename set:
#   (1) TOOLS keep free argv but are identified by RESOLVED PATH + sha256 against the measured tool set;
#   (2) WRAPPERS are a CLOSED FORM SET — an interpreter start is allowed only when its whole argv equals one of the
#       measured forms, and stdin to a wrapper is red unconditionally;
#   (3) argv, stdin CONTENT and the env passed to the child are scanned together for old-plan pointers.
ALLOWED_LIVE_TOOLS = frozenset({"git"})
ALLOWED_LIVE_WRAPPERS = frozenset({"env", "sh", "python3.12"})
ALLOWED_LIVE_BINARIES = ALLOWED_LIVE_TOOLS | ALLOWED_LIVE_WRAPPERS
# Measured wrapper forms: the two legitimate runtime probes review v11 measured as false reds. Anything else is red.
ALLOWED_LIVE_WRAPPER_FORMS = (("env", "true"), ("python3.12", "-c", "print(1)"))
